laurel 2780: IPA v4.2 AP side (step 2 of cellular, docs/laurel_sprout/cellular.md section 6). New: bsd/dev/laurel_ext4.c + laurel_ext4_dir.c (read-only ext4 reader for the vendor partition), laurel_ipa_regs.h (addresses, registers, memory layout, QMI ids), laurel_ipa_hw.c (RPM IPA clock 201 MHz, SMMU SIDs 0xE0/0xE2 identity, ipa3_init_hw registers incl. BCR = 0, TX_CFG bit 12 cleared, IDLE_INDICATION_CFG = 256; after the firmware the v4.2 local memory tables through the SRAM direct window, SMEM item 497), laurel_ipa_fw.c (ipa_fws.mdt + .bNN from vendor_<active slot> through the ext4 reader, then the shared PAS loader of laurel 2775 with PAS 15 = trinket.dtsi qcom,ipa_fws qcom,pas-id <0xf>, region pil_ipa_fw_mem 0x57500000 + 0x10000), laurel_ipa_qmi.c (QMI 0x31 messages, pure, host-tested), laurel_ipa.c (IPA thread at modem READY: clock -> SMMU -> registers -> firmware -> GSI_STATUS bit 0 -> local memory -> SMEM 497; then in the modem watch thread NEW_SERVER 0x31:0x101 at port 0x4015, INIT_MODEM_DRIVER from port 0x4016 to the modem's 0x31:0x201, answers INDICATION_REGISTER / INSTALL_FILTER_RULE / FILTER_INSTALLED_NOTIF / CONFIG / INIT_MODEM_DRIVER_CMPLT, MASTER_DRIVER_INIT_COMPLETE indication; state on after the INIT_MODEM_DRIVER answer + CMPLT; one line 'LAUREL IPA: on|off: reason', sysctl kern.laurel_ipa, kill switch ipa=0). TopazModem.cpp: laurel_ipa_server/_rx/_poll hooks next to the laurel_cell ones, topaz_qrtr_new_server(), SMP2P 'ipa' answer from laurel_ipa_smp2p_answer() (3 = valid + AP clock on once the RPM vote is acked, else 1 as before), laurel_ipa_off() at every laurel_cell_off() (modem crash, watch end, modem=0, SoC map, PAS boot, GLINK): off, no restart. laurel_cell.c: the fixed ipa_up is now laurel_ipa_state(): SET_OPERATING_MODE online only when the IPA is on; the radio-off reason is the IPA's.

